{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on a9197346, R16 refusals under older pinned destinations: yes, as you propose.\n\n1. Under an older pinned destination, the host checks reserved paths and declared prefixes before the provider push. A refused publication records the existing outcome, {send:'not-sent', seen:\u003cactual head\u003e}, with the existing reason host-refused through seenDecides. No pinned rule, outcome shape or replay changes.\n2. The host's answer to the caller names the specific cause: the reserved path, or the prefix that the package did not declare. The record holds only host-refused, because the old schema has no field for the cause.\n3. The new destination version records the specific publication-policy reason in the journal.\n4. Never write a fabricated absent result or any other evidence to make an old judge refuse. A truthful generic reason is better than a fake specific one.\n\nThis amends R16 item 3 for older pins: \"recorded with a reason\" means host-refused in the journal, with the cause in the host answer. Witnesses under an older pin: the journal shows host-refused, and the answer names reserved path or undeclared prefix. Under the new version, the journal shows the specific reason. Name both behaviors in the head report and in the fold publication note's section 6."}